<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.982 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.982 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.2 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due September 4 was 2.982 percent, down from 3.005 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 182-day T-bills due December 4, 1997 was 3.312 percent, down from 3.392 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due June 28, 1998 was 3.787 percent, down from 3.868 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$600 million three-month, C$125 million six-month and C$125 million one-year bills. It holds C$575 million of C$5.6 billion bills due June 12. (Details follow)  </p>
